      "title": "Determining Whether Two Vectors are Parallel"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b68aa7fa-5f84-5372-bdc2-c4e43d2380e6",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $\\lambda (\\frac{2}{5}\\mathbf{a} - \\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b})$ and $4\\mathbf{a} - 25\\mathbf{b}$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n4\\mathbf{a} - 25\\mathbf{b}=\\lambda (\\frac{2}{5}\\mathbf{a} - \\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n10(\\frac{2}{5}\\mathbf{a} - \\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b})=\\lambda (\\frac{2}{5}\\mathbf{a} - \\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(\\frac{2}{5}\\mathbf{a} - \\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b})$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2}{5}\\mathbf{a} - \\frac{5}{2}\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n10\\,u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nSince $u$ is non-zero,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=10.\n$$",
