    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0e188dc8-0a45-54fc-9fe4-f57e1da468a2",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $\\lambda (3\\mathbf{a} - 3 \\sqrt{13}\\mathbf{b})$ and $- 9 \\sqrt{13}\\mathbf{a} + 117\\mathbf{b}$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$\n\n$\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n- 9 \\sqrt{13}\\mathbf{a} + 117\\mathbf{b}=\\lambda (3\\mathbf{a} - 3 \\sqrt{13}\\mathbf{b}).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n- 3 \\sqrt{13}(3\\mathbf{a} - 3 \\sqrt{13}\\mathbf{b})=\\lambda (3\\mathbf{a} - 3 \\sqrt{13}\\mathbf{b}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(3\\mathbf{a} - 3 \\sqrt{13}\\mathbf{b})$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=3\\mathbf{a} - 3 \\sqrt{13}\\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n- 3 \\sqrt{13}\\,u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nSince $u$ is non-zero,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=- 3 \\sqrt{13}.\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "90bf0bbf-790e-5413-b371-31649ec5b94b",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "9c6ebedf-3a27-535b-a5b9-c71dbab3df30",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "- 3 \\sqrt{13}"
            }
          ],
